from pathlib import Path
import pandas as pd,numpy as np
O=Path(__file__).parent;s=pd.read_csv(O/'strict_338.csv').set_index('Record_ID');checks=[]
for name in ['extended_948','exploratory_989']:
 q=pd.read_csv(O/f'{name}.csv');q=q[q.Record_ID.isin(s.index)].set_index('Record_ID');cols=['DOI','Canonical_Molecular_ID','Retention_Final','calculated_concentration_ratio_percent']
 checks.append({'comparison':name,'strict_rows':len(s),'embedded_rows':len(q),'ids_identical':set(q.index)==set(s.index),'target_identical':np.allclose(q.calculated_concentration_ratio_percent.sort_index(),s.calculated_concentration_ratio_percent.sort_index()),'key_features_identical':q[cols].sort_index().equals(s[cols].sort_index()),'note':'Predictions are expected to differ across tiers because training data differ.'})
pd.DataFrame(checks).to_csv(O/'common_338_reproducibility.csv',index=False)
m=pd.read_csv(O/'summary_metrics.csv');table=m[['tier','design','n_test','test_groups','mean_fold_r2','sd_fold_r2','r2','mae','rmse','eligible_rows','excluded_unreliable_source']].to_markdown(index=False)
text='# Final comparison report\n\n## Integrity\nAll requested tiers have exactly 338, 948, and 989 records with no missing target or duplicate record ID. Strict rows are verified; extended and exploratory rows retain their weaker evidence classifications.\n\n## Fixed protocol\nHistorical XGBoost: 450 estimators, depth 3, learning rate 0.03, min child weight 3, subsample/colsample 0.8, L2 5, seed 42; log1p target; fold-local median/scaling and one-hot preprocessing; five-fold GroupKFold. Target is apparent concentration ratio, not mass retention.\n\n## Results\n\n'+table+'\n\nMolecular grouping has zero molecular overlap but recorded DOI overlap per fold. Source-held-out splits group by stored DOI; exploratory excludes 18 DOI-conflict rows (971 eligible), while strict and extended have 338 and 948 eligible rows.\n\n## Interpretation\nThe extended tier increases molecular-CV pooled R² relative to strict, but source-held-out pooled R² remains negative. Exploratory has poorer molecular pooled R² and only near-zero source-held-out pooled R²; it is not fully verified. Strict is small (6 DOI groups) and highly unstable. Carry forward the strict tier for evidence-critical claims, using the extended tier only as explicitly labelled exploratory sensitivity/training data; do not deploy any tier.\n';(O/'FINAL_COMPARISON_REPORT.md').write_text(text);(O/'README.md').write_text('Run run_analysis.py, then finish_reports.py. Both read existing Stage A data and write only this directory.\n')
